{#
mail/unified_all_mail.html.twig — All Mail across the reader's accounts.
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Every conversation outside Spam and the bin, archived mail included: the list
archived mail has to be browsed in. Opt-in — its sidebar row is the All Mail
label, created hidden and switched on in label settings (LabelRole::AllMail).

Scope `all_mail` with an empty value, which is how the toolbar, a row's
buttons and "select all" tell the server which list they were pressed in;
an account's own All Mail carries the account id instead
(mail/all_mail.html.twig, AllMailView).

One list, no category tabs, as Unread: everything together is the point.
#}
{% extends '_layout/_mailbox.html.twig' %}

{% block list_scope %}all_mail{% endblock %}

{% block title %}{{ 'sidebar.nav.all_mail'|trans }} — {{ 'app.name'|trans }}{% endblock %}

{% block inbox_tabs %}
    <div class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-line">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink-soft">{{ 'sidebar.nav.all_mail'|trans }}</h2>
    </div>
{% endblock %}

{% block message_list %}
    {% if threads is empty %}
        <li class="px-4 py-8 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint">
            {{ 'all_mail.empty'|trans }}
        </li>
    {% else %}
        {% for thread in threads %}
            {# The account dot, as on the unified Inbox: rows from every
               account sit side by side here. #}
            {% include '_partials/_thread_row.html.twig' with { thread: thread, unified: true } %}
        {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
